===Etymology===
{{ety|en|id=pigment fluid|:inh|enm:ynke<id:ink>}}

From {{inh|en|enm|ynke}}, from {{der|en|fro|enque}}, from {{der|en|la|encaustum|t=purple ink used by Roman emperors to sign documents}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἔγκαυστον|t=burned-in}}, from {{m|grc|ἐν|t=in}} + {{m|grc|καίω|t=burn}}. In this sense, displaced native {{ncog|ang|blæc||ink|lit=black}}.

Sense four refers to the ink used in [[newspaper|newspapers]].

